  ('362155125303636933', 'Juan Moreira', 1973, 'History, Drama, Western', 'Leonardo Favio', 'Jorge Zuhair Jury, Leonardo Favio', 'Rodolfo Bebán, Pablo Cumo, Edgardo Suárez, Jorge Villalba, Carlos Muñoz Arosa, Elcira Olivera Garcés, Alba Mugica, Eduardo Rudy', null, 'In the late nineteenth century, the mule driver Juan Moreira is a good gaucho and worker who, like many others, is subjected to abuse and humiliation by the powerful, either the police or landowners.', 'In the late nineteenth century, the mule driver Juan Moreira is a good gaucho and worker who, like many others, is subjected to abuse and humiliation by the powerful, either the police or landowners.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/s0B0damR2mmyOPFOvM2JCKZjy0b.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:127467'),
  ('403984030959949929', 'Juan of the Dead', 2011, 'Horror, Comedy', 'Alejandro Brugués, Carles Gusi, Laura Alvea', 'Alejandro Brugués', 'Alexis Díaz de Villegas, Jorge Molina, Andros Perugorría, Andrea Duro, Jazz Vilá, Eliecer Ramírez, Blanca Rosa Blanco, Susana Pous', 'NR', 'While Havana is full of zombies hungry for human flesh, official media reported that the disturbances are caused by dissidents paid by the United States. Panic seizes all until Juan comes to the rescue: he discovers he can kill the undead destroying his brain, and decides to start a small business under the slogan "We kill your loved ones."', 'While Havana is full of zombies hungry for human flesh, official media reported that the disturbances are caused by dissidents paid by the United States. Panic seizes all until Juan comes to the rescue: he discovers he can kill the undead destroying his brain, and decides to start a small business under the slogan "We kill your loved ones."', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/6s8N9k2QWXMt57amIONEnDgiYjJ.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:74726'),
  ('1055342989343988719', 'Juan, I Forgot I Don''t Remember', 1999, 'Documentary', 'Juan Carlos Rulfo', null, 'Juan José Arreola, Manuel Cosío, Clara Aparicio de Rulfo, Rebeca Jiménez, Justo Peralta, Jesus Ramirez', null, 'Juan Carlos Rulfo, the son of the acclaimed Mexican writer and photographer Juan Rulfo, travels to the plains of Jalisco in search of information on his father. What starts as a tribute to a great artist, however, becomes a meditation on aging and how it''s affecting the history of a generation of great Mexican literature.', 'Juan Carlos Rulfo, the son of the acclaimed Mexican writer and photographer Juan Rulfo, travels to the plains of Jalisco in search of information on his father. What starts as a tribute to a great artist, however, becomes a meditation on aging and how it''s affecting the history of a generation of great Mexican literature.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/12ZV8IZPWSrh3zAzfMAQX2UYOKf.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:214952'),
  ('977860111163840887', 'Juana Azurduy, Guerrillera de la Patria Grande', 2016, 'History', 'Jorge Sanjinés', null, 'Piti Campos, Fernando Arze, Cristian Mercado, Jorge Hidalgo, Luis Aduviri, Gina Alcon', null, 'Doña Juana Azurduy, widow of Padilla, is visited in November 1825 by the liberators Simón Bolívar and Antonio José de Sucre in the city of Chuquisaca.', 'Doña Juana Azurduy, widow of Padilla, is visited in November 1825 by the liberators Simón Bolívar and Antonio José de Sucre in the city of Chuquisaca.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/c3GuzCwQPqQGnb5JWmVkkB6iHS5.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:541556'),
